The blocks add surface exclusions beyond Z-2 (`no shop/menu boards, no readable labels, no price tags, no book/journal page text`) — that part is stronger than required. The defect is the three missing tokens/clause. `letters`/`numbers` are not cosmetic here: Concept 1/3 sit at a chai stall and a market lane, scenes that naturally carry prices and menu boards — the exact AAR-14 chalkboard-menu failure class. AAR-25 Z-5 is explicit: compliance is measured on delivered bytes; "the prompt asked for no text" is not evidence.

